WEBVTT

00:00:08.417 --> 00:00:10.376
[squawks]

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.160
Genius.

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:14.293
[grunting]

00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:19.254
Genius! Genius!

00:00:19.428 --> 00:00:21.256
Genius!

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.868
[chanting]:
Genius! Genius! Genius!

00:00:25.304 --> 00:00:26.522
[Dawn and Guy laughing]

00:00:26.697 --> 00:00:27.915
PHIL and HOPE:
Genius.

00:00:31.919 --> 00:00:34.618
[sighs]:
Genius. Mm.

00:00:40.362 --> 00:00:41.929
-Boom.
-Boom.

00:00:42.103 --> 00:00:43.975
[sighs]
Couldn't sleep last night.

00:00:44.149 --> 00:00:45.411
-Me, neither.
-[back cracks]

00:00:45.585 --> 00:00:47.326
When I woke up,
your mom was missing.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.285
You don't think
a predator took her, do you?

00:00:50.459 --> 00:00:51.504
Nope. Found her.

00:00:52.853 --> 00:00:54.115
[Ugga sighs]

00:00:54.289 --> 00:00:55.639
[Sandy squeals]

00:00:55.813 --> 00:00:57.466
It's like this place is
changing everyone.

00:00:57.641 --> 00:00:58.990
We don't sleep-pile anymore.

00:00:59.164 --> 00:01:00.556
We don't wake up together.

00:01:00.731 --> 00:01:03.385
And Thunk just stares
at that box.

00:01:03.559 --> 00:01:04.822
THUNK [moans]:
Oh.

00:01:04.996 --> 00:01:06.388
Not now, Douglas.

00:01:06.562 --> 00:01:08.347
-The birds are on.
-[whimpers]

00:01:08.521 --> 00:01:11.089
Dad, relax.
It's been one night.

00:01:11.263 --> 00:01:13.482
And a little change can be--
Guy?!

00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:16.485
♪ ♪

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:17.486
Hey.

00:01:17.661 --> 00:01:19.401
-Guy?
-Wow.

00:01:19.575 --> 00:01:23.275
You're you,
but you don't look like you.

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:24.363
[sniffs]

00:01:24.537 --> 00:01:25.930
And you smell like
flowers and...

00:01:26.104 --> 00:01:27.932
-And soft rain.
-[sniffs]

00:01:28.106 --> 00:01:29.847
More like
a clear mountain stream.

00:01:30.021 --> 00:01:31.762
With just a hint of vanilla.

00:01:31.936 --> 00:01:34.373
It's called a shower.
You should try it.

00:01:34.547 --> 00:01:37.289
You want me
to smell like vanilla?

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:38.638
Just a hint.

00:01:38.812 --> 00:01:40.335
What happened to your clothes?

00:01:40.509 --> 00:01:42.120
Oh, we burned his clothes
while he was in the shower.

00:01:42.294 --> 00:01:44.383
In fact, they were so dirty

00:01:44.557 --> 00:01:46.646
that we washed them
and then burned them.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.126
[laughter]

00:01:49.214 --> 00:01:51.042
[distorted laughter]

00:01:51.216 --> 00:01:53.000
[laughter]

00:01:53.174 --> 00:01:54.959
Come on, Thunk.
We're going outside.

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:57.222
[whining]: I don't wanna.
I'm watching birds.

00:01:57.396 --> 00:02:00.181
In my day, we didn't stare
at birds; we fought them.

00:02:00.355 --> 00:02:01.182
Let me live my life!

00:02:01.356 --> 00:02:02.836
Hey, new friend girl.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.709
-Want some breakfast?
-Um, sure.

00:02:05.883 --> 00:02:06.971
Oh. I'll start the fire again.

00:02:07.145 --> 00:02:08.146
Fire.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.452
["True" by Spandau Ballet
playing]

00:02:10.626 --> 00:02:11.845
[giggles]

00:02:12.019 --> 00:02:13.629
-Hey.
-Hey, yeah.

00:02:13.804 --> 00:02:16.328
-Check this out. [grunts]
-[music slows, stops]

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:20.419
Now, that's how you make a fire.

00:02:20.593 --> 00:02:22.116
You don't need
two people anymore.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.683
I can't believe how much time
I wasted clacking rocks.

00:02:23.857 --> 00:02:25.337
This is amazing.

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:28.340
And it's such a time-saver,
and it's so simple.

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:30.255
No more smashed fingers.

00:02:30.429 --> 00:02:31.691
[fading]: The Bettermans
really do have...

00:02:31.865 --> 00:02:33.867
[birds calling]

00:02:40.744 --> 00:02:42.528
[chuckling]:
Oh, there you are.

00:02:42.702 --> 00:02:45.400
I was looking all over for you--

00:02:45.574 --> 00:02:46.532
Whoa.

00:02:46.706 --> 00:02:48.621
We are really up here.

00:02:48.795 --> 00:02:51.493
Do I smell weird to you?

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:52.581
[sniffs]

00:02:52.756 --> 00:02:54.453
You smell different.

00:02:54.627 --> 00:02:57.064
Like [sniffs] river rocks
with a... [sniffs]

00:02:57.238 --> 00:02:58.370
hint of moss.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:02:59.850
[sniffs]

00:03:00.024 --> 00:03:01.808
Whoa.
What's that mark on your wrist?

00:03:01.982 --> 00:03:03.679
Oh, it's just a scar.

00:03:03.854 --> 00:03:04.768
Scar?

00:03:04.942 --> 00:03:06.160
Yeah, from a thorned crab.

00:03:06.334 --> 00:03:07.335
No big deal.

00:03:07.509 --> 00:03:08.989
Whoa. [chuckles]
And that?

00:03:09.163 --> 00:03:10.643
Razor worm.

00:03:10.817 --> 00:03:12.645
-Well, what about that one?
-Scorpion badger.

00:03:12.819 --> 00:03:15.300
Swamp snake, sky snake, volcano,

00:03:15.474 --> 00:03:16.562
end of the world, [chuckles]

00:03:16.736 --> 00:03:18.651
my little sister,
my little sister,

00:03:18.825 --> 00:03:20.174
my little sister--
She bites a lot.

00:03:20.348 --> 00:03:22.611
And my dad doesn't even know
about this one.

00:03:22.786 --> 00:03:24.962
Whoa. Peanut toe.

00:03:25.136 --> 00:03:26.485
[Sash sighs weakly]

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:30.010
Every mark is an adventure.
[sighs]

00:03:30.184 --> 00:03:32.621
My parents
won't even let me have scars.

00:03:32.796 --> 00:03:34.101
That's why they built the wall.

00:03:34.275 --> 00:03:35.929
To keep me safe.

00:03:38.714 --> 00:03:39.672
EEP:
You're not allowed

00:03:39.846 --> 00:03:41.500
-outside the wall?
-Nope.

00:03:41.674 --> 00:03:44.285
Not since what happened
to Guy's family.

00:03:44.459 --> 00:03:48.115
So, this farm...

00:03:48.289 --> 00:03:50.596
is like your cave.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:52.816
You're just like me.

00:03:53.773 --> 00:03:54.818
Come on.

00:03:56.254 --> 00:03:57.516
-[low growling]
-Oh, man.

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:59.518
Is this your ride?

00:03:59.692 --> 00:04:00.954
Nah, it's my dad's.

00:04:02.173 --> 00:04:03.827
[loud purring]

00:04:05.916 --> 00:04:07.918
Listen to this baby purr.

00:04:08.092 --> 00:04:09.310
See that pig gator over there?

00:04:09.484 --> 00:04:10.572
Yeah.

00:04:10.746 --> 00:04:12.444
-Want to jump it?
-Yeah.

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:14.098
[growls]

00:04:14.272 --> 00:04:16.187
-[whooping]
-[pig gator snorts]

00:04:16.361 --> 00:04:18.145
-See that chicken seal
over there? -Yeah.

00:04:18.319 --> 00:04:20.017
-Want to jump it?
-Yeah!

00:04:20.191 --> 00:04:21.888
-[whooping]
-[crows]

00:04:22.062 --> 00:04:23.281
You see that wall?

00:04:23.455 --> 00:04:24.543
-Yeah.
-Want to jump it?

00:04:24.717 --> 00:04:25.892
Yeah!

00:04:26.066 --> 00:04:28.199
No! Eep, I'm not allowed to go

00:04:28.373 --> 00:04:30.114
-outside the wall!
-Don't worry.

00:04:30.288 --> 00:04:31.898
We'll be back
before anyone knows.

00:04:32.072 --> 00:04:35.162
♪ ♪

00:04:37.773 --> 00:04:39.863
[roaring]

00:04:42.082 --> 00:04:44.084
[shouting]

00:04:44.258 --> 00:04:45.781
[grunting]

00:04:45.956 --> 00:04:47.348
[panting heavily]

00:04:48.697 --> 00:04:50.221
Are you okay?

00:04:50.395 --> 00:04:52.614
Woo-hoo!

00:04:52.788 --> 00:04:54.660
Oh, my gosh!
My heart is pounding!

00:04:54.834 --> 00:04:56.792
I feel so alive!

00:04:56.967 --> 00:04:59.795
Let's jump more stuff.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:01.580
[whooping]

00:05:02.711 --> 00:05:03.756
[snorts]

00:05:04.844 --> 00:05:06.106
-Ready?
-[squeaking]

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.107
Let's do it.

00:05:07.281 --> 00:05:08.108
[grunts]

00:05:08.282 --> 00:05:09.588
-[grunts]
-[flushing]

00:05:09.762 --> 00:05:11.503
-Yeah! [laughs]
-[cheering]

00:05:11.677 --> 00:05:12.852
Again.
Something bigger.

00:05:13.026 --> 00:05:14.245
Uh...

00:05:14.419 --> 00:05:16.160
Oh. Mrs. Betterman.

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:17.726
We were just checking out
this invention.

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:19.076
Wh-What's it for?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.947
-Um... it...
-[flushing] -[squeaking]

00:05:21.121 --> 00:05:23.602
W-- You know,
why don't you ask Phil?

00:05:23.776 --> 00:05:25.691
He-he spends
a lot of time in there.

00:05:25.865 --> 00:05:28.955
[chuckles softly]
Anyway, um, here.

00:05:29.129 --> 00:05:30.914
I thought
you might want to have this.

00:05:31.088 --> 00:05:34.569
It's some old pictures
of our families.

00:05:34.743 --> 00:05:36.397
Oh.

00:05:36.571 --> 00:05:38.660
Thank you.

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:39.661
[flushing]

00:05:39.835 --> 00:05:40.662
[shouting]

00:05:40.836 --> 00:05:42.316
[cheers]

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:43.578
-Where does this go?
-[whimpers]

00:05:43.752 --> 00:05:46.581
But, Dad,
what if I miss something?

00:05:46.755 --> 00:05:47.756
I want to go back inside.

00:05:47.931 --> 00:05:48.932
No, Thunk.

00:05:49.106 --> 00:05:50.020
Play with Douglas.

00:05:50.194 --> 00:05:51.195
He's feeling left out.

00:05:51.369 --> 00:05:52.500
And he's sad that everyone

00:05:52.674 --> 00:05:54.676
isn't spending time together
anymore!

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:55.895
[panting]

00:05:56.069 --> 00:05:56.983
[Thunk sighs]

00:05:57.157 --> 00:05:58.028
All right.

00:05:58.202 --> 00:05:59.203
You want to play fetch, Douglas?

00:05:59.377 --> 00:06:01.727
-[barking]
-Yeah. Okay.

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:02.989
Okay. Go get it!

00:06:03.163 --> 00:06:04.773
-[squawking]
-Oh!

00:06:04.948 --> 00:06:07.167
I'm sorry! I'm sorry,
I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:06:07.341 --> 00:06:09.256
I'm going back to the window!

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.389
[groans]

00:06:11.563 --> 00:06:13.086
PHIL [chuckles]:
Hey! There he is.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:14.653
-[groans loudly]
-Grug!

00:06:14.827 --> 00:06:16.176
Over here, buddy.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:17.830
Let's go for a ride.

00:06:18.004 --> 00:06:20.267
Grug. Gruggers.

00:06:20.441 --> 00:06:21.486
G-G-G-Grug.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.575
-[grunts]
-Grug. [screaming]

00:06:23.749 --> 00:06:25.925
Grug? Grug.

00:06:26.099 --> 00:06:27.927
Want to go for that ride?

00:06:28.101 --> 00:06:29.581
Pretty impressive, eh, Grug?

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:31.539
Funny story--

00:06:31.713 --> 00:06:33.933
everything you see before you
used to be

00:06:34.107 --> 00:06:37.023
a sad, hopeless,
dust-filled wasteland.

00:06:37.197 --> 00:06:38.416
That doesn't sound funny.

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.809
But through the power
of higher thought,

00:06:40.984 --> 00:06:43.116
I devised a way
to get all the water

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:46.163
from that high mountain source
to flow down here.

00:06:46.337 --> 00:06:47.860
-GRUG: How interesting.
-Yep.

00:06:48.034 --> 00:06:51.081
-I turned a barren desert
into a lush oasis. -[sighs]

00:06:51.255 --> 00:06:53.474
Now we have all the water
we need and then some.

00:06:53.648 --> 00:06:55.215
-[groans loudly]
-Matter of fact, we're thinking

00:06:55.389 --> 00:06:57.087
of putting in a new waterfall
feature right over there.

00:06:57.261 --> 00:06:58.784
-Ooh. Banana.
-No!

00:06:58.958 --> 00:07:00.873
Ow! [exhales]
What'd you do that for?

00:07:01.047 --> 00:07:04.311
Sorry. I'm afraid I must
remind you of our one rule.

00:07:04.485 --> 00:07:06.270
We don't eat the bananas.

00:07:06.444 --> 00:07:07.532
Well, why not?

00:07:07.706 --> 00:07:09.534
I mean, they're everywhere!

00:07:09.708 --> 00:07:12.145
Look! You got a whole bowl
full of 'em over there.

00:07:12.319 --> 00:07:15.105
-Who are those for? -Grug, we
could talk about fruit all day.

00:07:15.279 --> 00:07:16.802
Or, uh...

00:07:16.976 --> 00:07:19.022
do you want to see
something really cool?

00:07:19.196 --> 00:07:21.807
GRUG:
I don't know.

00:07:21.981 --> 00:07:22.851
[squealing]

00:07:23.026 --> 00:07:25.028
Whoa!
[laughing]

